256
00:11:40.560 --> 00:11:44.300
So, it just felt a lot better to spread it out over two.

257
00:11:44.300 --> 00:11:51.860
And another part about that storyline was that it was pairings.

258
00:11:52.260 --> 00:12:01.620
And, you know, a writing exercise that I often did with the writers was I'd have them try and come up with pairings of characters that we hadn't had scenes together before.

259
00:12:01.840 --> 00:12:08.820
And so, this entire episode was fun pairings like Ryan and Stanley or Phyllis and Karen.

260
00:12:10.100 --> 00:12:20.540
And, of course, Angela and Pam, who have a great emotional storyline where they really are kind of growing as friends.

261
00:12:20.920 --> 00:12:25.780
And it was really cool to see Jim and Dwight, too, and see their backstory.

262
00:12:25.780 --> 00:12:35.140
And then the other thing about Traveling Salesman was we used in the client, we used being good at sales to make Michael more likable.

263
00:12:35.140 --> 00:12:41.480
And, you know, in Traveling Salesman, you see a whole bunch of different characters and how they are as salespeople.

264
00:12:42.020 --> 00:12:52.560
