286
00:14:14.020 --> 00:14:22.600
So, for this episode, because we actually shot it in conjunction with The Return, we did something called crossboarding.

287
00:14:22.900 --> 00:14:26.660
It's a little lingo that they use in the biz.

288
00:14:31.900 --> 00:14:35.500
So, crossboarding is when you shoot two episodes at once.

289
00:14:35.660 --> 00:14:46.780
We normally shot one episode each week, but we shot these episodes over a 10-day period from October 16, 2006 to October 27, 2006.

290
00:14:47.440 --> 00:14:51.680
And the main reason for this was because of locations.

291
00:14:53.020 --> 00:15:00.500
We just had a lot of places to go in these two episodes, and having the flexibility to shoot it over a two-week period was really helpful.

292
00:15:00.860 --> 00:15:03.080
Yes, and they would also do a thing, you guys.

293
00:15:03.220 --> 00:15:05.120
They call it shooting out a location.

294
00:15:05.340 --> 00:15:11.680
So, for example, every scene that happened in that coffee shop, they would film in one day.

295
00:15:11.700 --> 00:15:13.700
And then they could close out that location.

296
00:15:13.700 --> 00:15:16.260
They don't have to pay for that location for multiple days.

297
00:15:16.260 --> 00:15:22.420
So, sometimes when you crossboard, it's a great way to save money because you can shoot out a location.

298
00:15:22.680 --> 00:15:23.040
Yes.

