He said in the script, it was just that Stanley is driving and laughing, and they just kind of let him go.

1239
01:00:48.120 --> 01:00:53.420
And he improvised the whole thing about, hi, hi, you sounded like my six-month-old niece.

1240
01:00:53.420 --> 01:00:55.720
And like all of that, Leslie was just riffing.

1241
01:00:56.340 --> 01:00:58.000
Oh, that was so good.

1242
01:00:58.320 --> 01:00:59.040
I know.

1243
01:00:59.040 --> 01:01:08.320
And he said, in fact, whenever Stanley would go off on Ryan, as he has throughout the show, they would just let Leslie just go.

1244
01:01:08.360 --> 01:01:10.760
And I think there's some amazing moments.

1245
01:01:11.180 --> 01:01:12.280
Oh, yes.

1246
01:01:12.500 --> 01:01:12.880
Yes.

1247
01:01:13.360 --> 01:01:18.260
Well, you know, and this is Ryan's second sales call now that has not gone well.

1248
01:01:18.520 --> 01:01:21.280
Remember, he went on the initiation sales call with Dwight.

1249
01:01:21.420 --> 01:01:22.680
They did not make the sale.

1250
01:01:22.820 --> 01:01:25.400
And now he's gone out on this call with Stanley.

1251
01:01:25.520 --> 01:01:27.800
Now, I believe Stanley's going to save the sale.

1252
01:01:27.800 --> 01:01:29.520
Oh, Stanley for sure saved it.

1253
01:01:29.740 --> 01:01:34.860
Okay, so while all of these sales meetings are happening, Pam and Angela are at the coffee shop.

1254
01:01:35.120 --> 01:01:46.660
Angela is in such a great mood, and she's telling Pam a story about how she had this friend who was in need, and this gallant man came to her rescue.

1255
01:01:47.100 --> 01:01:54.840
Yeah, she's like, he must really care for her a lot because he did this wonderful thing for my friend.

1256
01:01:55.300 --> 01:01:57.140
Yeah, she's talking in code.

1257
01:01:57.800 --> 01:01:59.080
She's speaking in code.

1258
01:01:59.300 --> 01:02:02.220
She's like, my friend, let's call her Noel.

1259
01:02:02.800 --> 01:02:06.020
And this gallant gentleman, we'll call him Kurt.

1260
01:02:06.840 --> 01:02:11.620
Well, we all know that Kurt is Dwight's middle name, right?

1261
01:02:11.960 --> 01:02:12.280
Yes.

1262
01:02:12.280 --> 01:02:14.920
And we got a lot of fan questions about this, Angela.

1263
01:02:15.500 --> 01:02:31.180
Kenzie B., Elizabeth R., Julia Lee, Nicole Fink, and Katie Kroll all want to know, when Angela refers to her friend Noel, is that because Noel is Angela's middle name?

1264
01:02:32.040 --> 01:02:36.000
It definitely sounds like a very Angela Martin middle name.

1265
01:02:36.560 --> 01:02:39.480
Well, yes, it is Angela's middle name.

1266
01:02:39.680 --> 01:02:44.440
Angela thinks she's being really savvy, but Pam totally knows who she's talking about.

1267
01:02:44.860 --> 01:02:46.760
But, yes, that is her middle name.

1268
01:02:46.860 --> 01:02:48.720
But, Jenna, I have a question for you.

1269
01:02:49.600 --> 01:02:50.000
Okay.

1270
01:02:50.100 --> 01:02:51.980
Is Noel in the script?

1271
01:02:52.180 --> 01:02:55.160
Because I have a little story about that middle name, and I'm curious.

1272
01:02:55.840 --> 01:02:58.540
I think what was in the script was Colette.

1273
01:02:59.540 --> 01:03:00.180
Okay.

1274
01:03:00.280 --> 01:03:06.840
I looked this up, and in the script, Angela actually says this.

1275
01:03:06.840 --> 01:03:13.320
She says, well, a friend of mine, let's just call her, oh, let's just call her me.

1276
01:03:13.880 --> 01:03:14.420
What?

1277
01:03:14.700 --> 01:03:15.700
And then you giggle.

1278
01:03:16.700 --> 01:03:17.340
Okay.

1279
01:03:17.340 --> 01:03:26.440
So, my memory of this is when we were shooting it that day, that the writers were pitching me different middle names, like different things to say.

1280
01:03:26.620 --> 01:03:28.860
I know in one of them it was Colette.

1281
01:03:28.980 --> 01:03:30.740
I have such a memory of saying that.

1282
01:03:32.120 --> 01:03:34.040
And then we said Noel.

1283
01:03:34.040 --> 01:03:39.900
And I like Noel the best because it sounds very sort of Angela Martin, doesn't it?

1284
01:03:39.900 --> 01:03:49.720
It's her love of Christmas, her love of the story of Christmas, that Noel would be her middle name, and that's the one we went with.

1285
01:03:50.100 --> 01:04:00.160
And Dave Rogers talks about it in the DVD commentary, and he goes, I remember it being Colette, and he thought maybe I improvised Noel, but I didn't.

1286
01:04:00.280 --> 01:04:01.400
That was a writer's pitch.

1287
01:04:01.580 --> 01:04:03.320
I mean, I think I was part of the dialogue.

1288
01:04:03.320 --> 01:04:07.260
I think we were pitching names, but that all sort of happened in the moment.

1289
01:04:07.680 --> 01:04:08.560
I love it.

1290
01:04:08.560 --> 01:04:09.740
It's perfect.

1291
01:04:10.180 --> 01:04:10.960
It's perfect.

1292
01:04:10.960 --> 01:04:17.120
It is such an Angela Noel Martin, and I believe that will appear on your wedding invitation.

1293
01:04:17.520 --> 01:04:18.240
Oh, yeah.

1294
01:04:18.480 --> 01:04:21.520
It's now part of my character's show Bible.

1295
01:04:22.220 --> 01:04:25.900
We had another fan catch in this scene, Angela.

1296
01:04:26.140 --> 01:04:30.660
Sarah Rouse wrote in to say, Pam is holding a piece of paper at the coffee shop.

1297
01:04:30.660 --> 01:04:33.400
What is that supposed to be, and what does it say?

1298
01:04:33.700 --> 01:04:37.560
Well, Sarah, that was the list of coffee orders.

1299
01:04:38.560 --> 01:04:40.140
From those deleted scenes.

1300
01:04:40.640 --> 01:04:45.440
I had all the coffee orders written down on that piece of paper, and I was going to use it to make my order.

1301
01:04:45.740 --> 01:04:54.600
Well, Angela, also in this scene, just because we were talking about it earlier, your flower hairdo is on full display.

1302
01:04:54.600 --> 01:05:02.160
Okay, just if you really want some great shots of it, guys, here it is, her WTF hairdo right here.

1303
01:05:02.560 --> 01:05:03.000
WTF.

1304
01:05:03.220 --> 01:05:03.920
Well, wait, wait.

1305
01:05:04.000 --> 01:05:04.860
I have something to share.

1306
01:05:04.860 --> 01:05:10.700
So, while we were on a break, I had been texting Kim Ferry about this hair, and she texted back.

1307
01:05:10.840 --> 01:05:13.060
And so, this is what she had to say about it.

1308
01:05:13.240 --> 01:05:15.840
I said, oh, my gosh, it's a real-time tidbit.

1309
01:05:16.040 --> 01:05:17.200
It's a real-time tidbit.

1310
01:05:17.200 --> 01:05:18.740
It just came in a few minutes ago.

1311
01:05:18.740 --> 01:05:24.360
So, I said, Kim, what was the inspiration for this bun?

1312
01:05:24.680 --> 01:05:30.660
I mean, I know that we thought my character was going to, like, be in a great mood, and so we wanted to try something new.

1313
01:05:30.680 --> 01:05:31.840
She said, yes.

1314
01:05:32.180 --> 01:05:33.740
Here is the inspiration.

1315
01:05:33.740 --> 01:05:40.480
She said, my first job in the business was working on a sci-fi show called Babylon 5.

1316
01:05:41.220 --> 01:05:50.260
I worked on this show for five years, and I couldn't use any contemporary hairstyles because they wanted the hairstyles to look futuristic.

1317
01:05:50.740 --> 01:06:02.340
So, I started coming up with all these different kind of braids and buns with wires and fancy updos and Zulu knots, basically anything different that I could think of.

1318
01:06:02.340 --> 01:06:10.160
And your bun with those fun swirls was a good one for me because I had done it on Babylon 5.

1319
01:06:10.500 --> 01:06:15.580
It's fast and easy, but technically, this is a sci-fi hairstyle.

1320
01:06:16.060 --> 01:06:16.680
Oh.

1321
01:06:17.060 --> 01:06:17.700
My.

1322
01:06:18.380 --> 01:06:19.020
Gosh.

1323
01:06:19.280 --> 01:06:20.480
Isn't that great?

1324
01:06:21.520 --> 01:06:25.360
Don't you feel like Dwight would have loved it because he was Mr. Sci-Fi?

1325
01:06:26.820 --> 01:06:27.460
Yes.

1326
01:06:27.460 --> 01:06:28.100
Yes.

1327
01:06:28.100 --> 01:06:31.640
No wonder she did her hair in this Babylon 5 hairstyle.

1328
01:06:32.340 --> 01:06:35.540
To thank Dwight for his, like, favor.

1329
01:06:36.020 --> 01:06:36.580
Yeah.

1330
01:06:36.820 --> 01:06:37.620
So, yes.

1331
01:06:37.800 --> 01:06:40.580
This hairstyle inspired by Babylon 5.

1332
01:06:40.660 --> 01:06:42.180
It's the sci-fi bun.

1333
01:06:43.760 --> 01:06:45.540
I don't think I could love that more.

1334
01:06:46.020 --> 01:06:48.100
Kim Ferry, thank you for the real-time tidbit.

1335
01:06:48.440 --> 01:06:49.440
Thank you, Kim Ferry.

1336
01:06:50.080 --> 01:06:53.120
Sam just wrote, beats Bears Babylon 5.

1337
01:06:54.340 --> 01:06:55.360
Beats, oh, wait.

1338
01:06:55.440 --> 01:06:55.820
Here we go.

1339
01:06:56.000 --> 01:06:58.640
Bears, Beats, Babylon 5, buns.

1340
01:06:59.080 --> 01:06:59.380
Oh.

1341
01:07:00.140 --> 01:07:00.740
Okay.

1342
01:07:00.840 --> 01:07:04.240
So, now, everybody is coming back from their sales calls.

1343
01:07:04.500 --> 01:07:05.280
Everyone's done.

1344
01:07:05.560 --> 01:07:10.680
And we have this amazing scene in the car with Karen and Phyllis.

1345
01:07:11.540 --> 01:07:15.380
Phyllis is so good in this scene because, you guys,

1346
01:07:15.380 --> 01:07:21.240
she is going to reveal such a big plot point and she just throws it away, right?

1347
01:07:21.620 --> 01:07:24.240
It's not, like, belabored in any way.

1348
01:07:24.260 --> 01:07:26.180
It's so perfect.

1349
01:07:27.060 --> 01:07:27.620
Yeah.

1350
01:07:28.000 --> 01:07:31.540
She's like, Karen, I had a lot of fun with you today.

1351
01:07:31.600 --> 01:07:33.460
I really enjoy spending time with you.

1352
01:07:33.620 --> 01:07:34.460
They're bonding.

1353
01:07:34.460 --> 01:07:35.620
They feel good.

1354
01:07:36.260 --> 01:07:39.080
And then she just very offhandedly says,

1355
01:07:39.340 --> 01:07:41.440
and I'm really glad you're with Jim.

1356
01:07:41.740 --> 01:07:44.660
It makes me really happy because, you know,

1357
01:07:44.800 --> 01:07:47.520
he was really hung up on Pam for such a long time.

1358
01:07:47.800 --> 01:07:49.800
And she's not even looking at Karen.

1359
01:07:49.960 --> 01:07:51.380
She's looking in a rearview mirror.

1360
01:07:51.520 --> 01:07:52.100
She's turning.

1361
01:07:52.300 --> 01:07:52.920
She's just driving.

1362
01:07:53.180 --> 01:07:55.240
She's sort of saying something off the cuff.

1363
01:07:55.400 --> 01:07:57.140
And it's that much more powerful.

1364
01:07:57.560 --> 01:08:03.120
And then Rashida, oh, my gosh, her reaction is so perfect.

1365
01:08:03.120 --> 01:08:03.260
Perfect.

1366
01:08:03.960 --> 01:08:05.860
It's a fantastic scene.

1367
01:08:06.060 --> 01:08:07.000
Fantastic scene.

1368
01:08:07.300 --> 01:08:10.760
I feel like her pulse stops for a second.

1369
01:08:10.940 --> 01:08:14.520
Like, I feel like I can see the wind go out of her, right?

1370
01:08:14.860 --> 01:08:16.440
Yes, I do, too.

1371
01:08:17.500 --> 01:08:20.900
You just, you see it hit her like a freight train,

1372
01:08:21.080 --> 01:08:25.460
but she can't react the way it's really hitting her.

1373
01:08:25.560 --> 01:08:26.860
It's so well done.

1374
01:08:26.860 --> 01:08:29.200
These ladies did such a great job.

1375
01:08:29.900 --> 01:08:30.880
I agree.

1376
01:08:31.380 --> 01:08:31.980
Yes.

1377
01:08:33.120 --> 01:08:36.500
Well, Andy is the first person to actually get back to the office.

1378
01:08:37.220 --> 01:08:42.080
And he starts, he starts sneaking around Dwight's desk.

1379
01:08:42.300 --> 01:08:43.740
He goes through his car.

1380
01:08:44.040 --> 01:08:45.640
Yeah, Andy is a total snake.

1381
01:08:45.900 --> 01:08:47.220
I mean, what the heck?

1382
01:08:47.360 --> 01:08:47.940
I know.

1383
01:08:48.140 --> 01:08:51.120
And he finds this toll booth receipt

1384
01:08:51.120 --> 01:08:54.380
that proves that Dwight was in New York this morning.

1385
01:08:54.640 --> 01:08:56.960
He didn't oversleep like he claimed.

1386
01:08:56.960 --> 01:08:58.500
And he marches into Michael's office.

1387
01:08:58.500 --> 01:09:01.100
And he's like, I found this toll booth receipt.

1388
01:09:01.700 --> 01:09:03.260
I wonder what he was doing.

1389
01:09:03.640 --> 01:09:05.740
Was he, maybe he was talking to Jan.

1390
01:09:06.060 --> 01:09:08.580
And then he says like, I seem to kind of remember.

1391
01:09:08.580 --> 01:09:13.820
I don't know who told me this, even though, Jenna, this was like, like an hour ago.

1392
01:09:14.000 --> 01:09:15.580
He's like, I don't know who told me this.

1393
01:09:15.700 --> 01:09:16.180
It was something.

1394
01:09:16.440 --> 01:09:20.520
And then he has maybe one of my favorite quotes of this episode.

1395
01:09:20.520 --> 01:09:21.780
He was like, there's a story.

1396
01:09:21.780 --> 01:09:22.280
I don't know.

1397
01:09:22.400 --> 01:09:24.620
It was about laundry and betrayal.

1398
01:09:25.500 --> 01:09:30.180
In my mind, this is now a lifetime movie called Laundry and Betrayal.

1399
01:09:30.180 --> 01:09:31.340
I want to see it.

1400
01:09:33.380 --> 01:09:33.900
Yes.

1401
01:09:34.480 --> 01:09:35.000
Yes.

1402
01:09:35.860 --> 01:09:37.040
Laundry and Betrayal.

1403
01:09:37.140 --> 01:09:38.240
I want to see this film.

1404
01:09:38.460 --> 01:09:38.960
I do too.

1405
01:09:39.660 --> 01:09:41.480
Well, so Michael calls Jan.

1406
01:09:42.920 --> 01:09:45.940
And Jan is like, well, I didn't speak to Dwight,

1407
01:09:46.040 --> 01:09:49.400
but he did not give a reason for why he was here.

1408
01:09:49.800 --> 01:09:50.180
Yes.

1409
01:09:50.320 --> 01:09:52.100
This is my kid's favorite part.

1410
01:09:52.260 --> 01:09:57.060
My kid's favorite part is Jan goes, he did sign into the security sign-in sheet,

1411
01:09:57.220 --> 01:09:59.880
but understate your business, he wrote.

1412
01:10:00.180 --> 01:10:02.660
Beeswax, not yours, Incorporated.

1413
01:10:03.000 --> 01:10:04.660
I love that too.

1414
01:10:04.740 --> 01:10:06.260
My kids loved that.

1415
01:10:06.480 --> 01:10:10.160
Well, when Dwight gets back to the office, Michael confronts him.

1416
01:10:11.160 --> 01:10:12.620
He's like, where were you?

1417
01:10:12.780 --> 01:10:13.560
Tell me where you were.

1418
01:10:13.680 --> 01:10:14.980
And Dwight will not say.

1419
01:10:15.040 --> 01:10:16.860
He won't say where he was.

1420
01:10:17.120 --> 01:10:18.140
He overslept.

1421
01:10:18.280 --> 01:10:19.420
The damn rooster didn't crow.

1422
01:10:20.360 --> 01:10:20.660
Yeah.

1423
01:10:21.420 --> 01:10:25.160
But he will not, he will not fess up.

1424
01:10:25.780 --> 01:10:27.420
And this becomes a problem.

1425
01:10:27.720 --> 01:10:29.120
And Pam knows why.

1426
01:10:29.760 --> 01:10:31.900
Pam and Angela are exchanging looks.

1427
01:10:32.080 --> 01:10:33.320
Angela is sweating it.

1428
01:10:33.540 --> 01:10:36.080
She's horrified that Dwight's going through this,

1429
01:10:36.120 --> 01:10:38.740
but she doesn't want people to know about them.

1430
01:10:38.960 --> 01:10:41.160
It's very layered emotionally for Angela.

1431
01:10:41.720 --> 01:10:48.060
Well, it leads to a break room scene with Dwight and Angela where you are, again, not facing one another.

1432
01:10:48.460 --> 01:10:51.660
One of your famous, famous break room scenes.

1433
01:10:51.940 --> 01:10:55.000
There's a little bit of heartbreak in the break room in this scene.

1434
01:10:55.000 --> 01:10:57.740
Oh, lady, I noticed it, too.

1435
01:10:58.240 --> 01:10:59.300
Here's what we had.

1436
01:10:59.560 --> 01:11:02.660
My mama knid me in a sexy sweater.

1437
01:11:15.760 --> 01:11:17.460
That was by Michelle Ferguson.

1438
01:11:17.760 --> 01:11:20.140
Michelle, you know how much we love that song.

1439
01:11:20.300 --> 01:11:21.060
We love it.

1440
01:11:21.580 --> 01:11:21.920
Yeah.

1441
01:11:22.200 --> 01:11:24.100
Michelle, I literally listen to it all the time.

1442
01:11:24.260 --> 01:11:25.400
It's super catchy.

1443
01:11:25.700 --> 01:11:26.820
It's very catchy.

1444
01:11:27.080 --> 01:11:27.900
I really love it.

1445
01:11:27.980 --> 01:11:29.620
Someone give this woman a music contract.

1446
01:11:30.060 --> 01:11:31.120
We'll buy it.

1447
01:11:31.240 --> 01:11:31.640
Okay.

1448
01:11:31.640 --> 01:11:33.000
We love it.

1449
01:11:33.360 --> 01:11:33.540
Yeah.

1450
01:11:33.860 --> 01:11:39.920
So Dwight is like, listen, why don't we just come clean and, you know, let people know our love for one another?

1451
01:11:40.180 --> 01:11:42.100
So this scene actually went on.

1452
01:11:42.280 --> 01:11:49.040
It's not in the deleted scenes, but we did shoot a little bit longer of a version where as I cry behind me,

1453
01:11:49.140 --> 01:11:51.020
Dwight's like, don't cry, monkey.

1454
01:11:51.720 --> 01:11:52.940
Monkeys don't cry.

1455
01:11:54.140 --> 01:11:56.760
Aw, I kind of wish that was still in there.

1456
01:11:56.900 --> 01:11:57.480
I know.

1457
01:11:57.680 --> 01:11:58.200
I know.

1458
01:11:58.200 --> 01:12:04.660
Well, Angela, a few people wrote in about this scene because they noted that when you start dating Andy,

1459
01:12:04.940 --> 01:12:07.740
you have no problem with everyone in the office knowing it.

1460
01:12:08.260 --> 01:12:12.140
Oh, well, Angela revenge dates Andy, you guys.

1461
01:12:12.540 --> 01:12:18.420
Andy's not her true love that she wants to protect and keep all to herself because it's so special.

1462
01:12:18.880 --> 01:12:22.680
She's starting to date Andy because she's mad as hell at Dwight.

1463
01:12:23.340 --> 01:12:23.900
Right.

1464
01:12:24.080 --> 01:12:25.260
Very different motivation.

1465
01:12:25.760 --> 01:12:26.040
Right.

1466
01:12:26.040 --> 01:12:35.240
In the meantime, Karen and Jim have gone to coffee and Karen is going to ask Jim if he had feelings for Pam.

1467
01:12:35.460 --> 01:12:37.700
And lady, I have a clip.

1468
01:12:38.100 --> 01:12:43.540
Sam, play the clip because everything you need to know is right here, Karen.

1469
01:12:43.880 --> 01:12:45.620
Why couldn't you hear it?

1470
01:12:46.360 --> 01:12:47.380
Let me ask you a question.

1471
01:12:47.660 --> 01:12:47.840
Okay.

1472
01:12:48.900 --> 01:12:50.680
Did you ever have a thing for Pam?

1473
01:12:51.540 --> 01:12:52.160
Pam?

1474
01:12:52.700 --> 01:12:54.700
Did I ever have a thing for her?

1475
01:12:55.180 --> 01:12:55.660
No.

1476
01:12:57.640 --> 01:12:58.460
Did she do something?

1477
01:13:00.540 --> 01:13:00.860
There.

1478
01:13:01.360 --> 01:13:03.260
That's all you need to know, Karen.

1479
01:13:03.600 --> 01:13:05.420
He clearly has a thing for her.

1480
01:13:05.660 --> 01:13:07.720
But, oh, poor Karen.

1481
01:13:07.940 --> 01:13:11.020
